# Deliberate bugs, one at a time: each (name, file, old text, new text) must make the suite fail.
# Run from the repo root:  python3 tests/mutation/mutate.py tests/mutation/mutants.py -- uv run pytest -x -q
# (the driver checks the suite is green first; do not edit the tree while it runs; each pattern must occur exactly once)
#
# Not listed, because they cannot change behaviour:
#  - search_filter: dropping `or date_str == UNKNOWN` (the text "unknown" falls through to `return date_str`, which is "unknown" again) and dropping
#    `or date_str.endswith("00:00")` (an ISO text without "+" or "Z" fails the strptime and falls through to the same result);
#  - positions.position_lock: skipping the explicit LOCK_UN (closing the file releases the lock);
#  - result_tools.calculate_portfolio_value: `shares >= 0` (a zero holding adds zero) and not skipping "CASH" (there is no CASH_price);
#  - result_tools.calculate_profit_loss_ratio: the `avg_loss == 0` guard (a negative return is never zero);
#  - price_tools.get_yesterday_profit: `shares >= 0` (a zero holding earns zero).
# Not run: main_parrallel `len(models) <= 1` -> `<= 0` would start real subprocesses from the test.

